ultiple orange yellow  lobulated areas measuring 0 7cm in greatest diameter  to 0 2cm in diameter  The remaining breast parenchyma consists of approximately 80  pink tan tissue with focal areas of grittiness  which focally abuts the posterior resection margin  Multiple cystic spaces  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  with smooth  pink tan lining are located in the mid medial anterior portion of the specimen  and come to REMOVED_DATE of the nearest anterior resection margin  No discrete masses are found  SECTION CODE  A  mid anterior margin  B  lateral anterior margin  C E  medial anterior margin  F  mid posterior margin  G  representative section through cystic space  medial section of specimen  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of tan yellow  fibroadipose tissue  The fatty tissue is dissected to reveal five  pink tan  irregular  ovoid shaped lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  SECTION CODE  H  five individual ovoid shaped soft tissue  I  remaining specimen submitted entirely  Resident  WEI LIEN WANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin Hughes MD PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT  SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 02 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast lesion                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   95    POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA    5   PRESENT AT INKED SURGICAL MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 0 8cm  in greatest dimension  Vascular invasion is not identified  Diagnosis by  Christophe Girardet  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 07                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with an attached localizing wire and accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing a gray  nodular area  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  which abuts the inked margin  The nodular area is submitted entirely in A and B  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in C through G  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS GROSS  RIGHT BREAST MASS   SUSPICIOUS LESION  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS O R  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 20 CLINICAL DATA  Inflammatory carcinoma  right breast  previous chemotherapy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SMALL FOCUS  2  FIBROSIS  GLANDULAR ATROPHY  SCAR  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION AND MULTINUCLEATED FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY SITE  3  ELEVEN AXILLARY LYMPH NODES WITH SINUS HISTIOCYTOSIS  AND NESTS OF BENIGN APPEARING NEVOMELANOCYTES IN ONE LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The inked resection margins are negative for carcinoma  A single lymph node shows numerous benign appearing nests of nevomelanocytic cells  This may be observed rarely as an incidental finding  however  the degree of involvement of this lymph node suggests the possibility of metastasis from a blue nevus or other melanocytic proliferation  Drs  Lynn Duncan and Martin Mihm have reviewed the lymph node slides and concur with the interpretation  Diagnosis by  Daniel Rubin  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 21                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in two containers  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  Right breast and axillary contents  is a 390 gm  23 x 15 x 3 5cm modified radical mastectomy partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 5cm skin ellipse containing a curved  2cm  well healed scar lateral to the areola  A long and a small black suture are attached to the specimen  designating the lateral and superior aspect  respectively  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing predominantly lobulated  yellow adipose tissue intermixed with gray white  fibrous breast parenchyma that is slightly firmer and with a gritty consistency in the region below the skin scar  The nipple and areola are unremarkable  The axillary adipose tissue is sectioned  revealing several tan pink  soft  grossly unremarkable lymph nodes measuring up to 1cm in greatest diameter  SECTION CODE  A B   breast and deep resection margin in the area underlying the scar C through G   breast parenchyma in the area underlying the scar H I   random sections from unremarkable breast J   nipple K   skin scar L M   axillary lymph nodes  Labeled  Right additional axillary tissue  is a 1 x 1 x 0 3cm piece of adipose tissue  Sectioning reveals a lymph node most of which has been replaced by fat  The specimen is bisected and submitted entirely in N  Resident  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  AMB GEN SURGICAL   ACC 4 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST WITH AXILLA PART B  RIGHT ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
