ary involvement  Lymphatic vessels  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL TISSUE   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT   MAMMOPLASTY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   FOCAL FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  LERWILL  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 14 28                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast and axillary content   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm attached axillary tail and a REMOVED_DATE x 4 2cm skin ellipse with an inverted nipple  There is a 2 5cm scar  1 8cm superior to the nipple  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm tan firm mass 0 1cm from the lateral  2 0cm from the posterior   0 1cm from the anterior  8 5cm from the medial  6 0cm from the superior and 5 5cm from the inferior margins  There is a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm tan nodule 1 0cm medial to the larger mass  that is 1cm or greater from the margins  There is a 3rd REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined tan hard nodule  4 0cm infero medial to the larger mass  that is 1cm greater from the margins  The remainder of the breast tissue is fibrofatty with no other lesions or masses identified  The axillary tail is serially dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows  A D  Largest mass  Mass  1   E  Mass  2 to anterior margin  F  Mass  2 to posterior margin  G  Fibrotic area between mass  1 and mass  2  H  Mass  3 to anterior margin  I J  Additional sections of mass  3  K  Fibrofatty tissue between mass  3 and mass  1  L  Fibrofatty tissue between mass  3 and mass  2  M  Two sections of fibrofatty tissue away from masses  N  Two lymph nodes from axillary tail  O  Two potential lymph nodes from the axillary tail  FF  Individual axillary lymph nodes  GG  Mass  1 to anterior margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary tissue   are multiple fragments of fibrofatty tissue aggregating to 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal 3 lymph nodes  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The larger node is bisected  and entirely submitted in cassette P  The two smaller ones are entirely submitted in cassette Q  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast additional superficial margin above tumor   are multiple fragments of tan fibrofatty tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes R S  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast tissue  is a 60gm aggregate of unremarkable grey to tan  pink skin with underlying fibrofatty tissue  The three fragments range from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  A representative section from each fragment is submitted as T U  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  is a 130gm  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm aggregate of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  Many of the fragments are covered by unremarkable grey tan to pink skin ranging from 3 9cm to 13 0cm in greatest dimension  Sectioning reveals focally dense grey white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted as V EE  Resident  NORMA RODRIGUEZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MG