Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 59 CLINICAL DATA  Status post left breast needle localization                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   A   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  99   REMOVED_DATE CM   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID TYPE  1    BREAST  LEFT   B   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95   0 6CM   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  PRESENT AT THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA  COMEDO TYPE  5    NOTE  Definitive lymphatic and vascular invasion is not present  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 01                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   A    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 03     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 10 19     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two parts  Labeled  Left breast mass  A inferior density  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm red and yellow  focally firm breast tissue fragments  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan  firm lesion with retracted borders focally abutting the inked margin  Representative section is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in A through G  with the lesion in A through D  Labeled  Posterior breast  calcification  B  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm red and yellow  focally firm breast fragment  inked and sectioned to reveal a hard  white material measuring R