mance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 10 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right modified radical mastectomy  long lateral  short stitch superior  is a 14 x 13 x 2cm mastectomy specimen with a 7 x 5 x 1cm axillary tail  Two sutures are present  short superior and long lateral  The nipple areolar complex is unremarkable  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a nodular and firm area  extending 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  It is REMOVED_DATE to 0 5cm from the closest  deep  resection margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A D  Firm area with posterior  deep  margin C F  Firm area with anterior margin G  Representative sections of uninvolved breast parenchyma The axillary content is dissected for lymph nodes  The largest node measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  which is submitted in cassette H after bisection  Additional lymph nodes are submitted in I M with I and J each containing one bisected lymph node  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  additional right axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 5cm aggregate of fatty tissue which is submitted entirely as cassette N  Resident  ZUOQIN TANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  AXILLA  ADDITIONAL RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
