ng  10  of the cut surfaces  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nipple to peripheral thickened skin to nearest margin  1 section cut in half    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of nipple  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of slightly firm area subjacent to nipple  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible previous biopsy site  to include gray white glistening posterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue between previous biopsy site and firm UOQ area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative firm UOQ area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative posterior margin  nearest to firm UOQ area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative LOQ  Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 25   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05 07 52PM ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were