he specimen  The short stitch marks the superior aspect of the specimen  The specimen is totally inked in black  and the superior aspect of the specimen is additionally inked in blue  Sectioning reveals a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and approaching the inferior margin of the specimen on the lateral side to 0 4cm  The walls of the biopsy cavity consist of fibrous tissue  The biopsy cavity is submitted in toto in cassette A through H  beginning at the lateral margin and proceeding to the medial margin  The area of closest approach to the resection margin is submitted in cassette A  Cassettes I through K  representative section of the rest of the specimen  Cassette L  skin ellipse submitted in toto  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents  is a piece of fatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Lymph nodes are bisected and submitted in cassettes M through P  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  separate superior nodule  are three pieces of hard  white tan tissue measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  Submitted in toto in cassettes Q and R  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  superior margin  additional   short  new superior margin  long  lateral   is a piece of fibrofatty tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The superior margin is marked by a short stitch  the lateral margin is marked by a long stitch  The specimen is inked in black in toto  The superior aspect is additionally inked in blue  The specimen is submitted in toto in cassettes S through Y  beginning at the lateral margin and proceeding to the medial margin  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   REEXCISION PART B  AXI