 with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localization wire  short stitch designating superior margin which is inked in black  long stitch designating lateral margin which is inked in blue  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm  white mass with peripheral retraction located 0 2cm from the inferior margin  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A through J with mass in G and H  No frozen section done  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are three parts  Labeled  additional inferior and lateral margin  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0 5cm fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked entirely in black  The superior margin is overlaid with blue  inferior is overlaid with red  lateral margin is overlaid with yellow and the anterior is overlaid with green  Sectioning to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely from lateral to medial in cassettes K through M  Labeled  final shaved margin  is an unoriented fragment of fatty adipose tissue measuring 3 x 3 x 0 5cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma except focal hemorrhagic areas  Entirely submitted in cassettes N through Q  Labeled  right axillary content  is a 6 x 5 x 2cm fatty adipose tissue  The lymph nodes are dissected and submitted entirely in cassettes R through T  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  FIRM  WHITE NODULE SUGGESTIVE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  LOCATED LESS THAN 1 MM FROM INKED INFERIOR MARGIN  NOT FROZEN  O R  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  Barbara Joyce Nath  M D  David Nathan Helman  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  INFERIOR   LATERAL    EXCISIONAL BI PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISIONAL B PART D  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION , Unchecked.
