Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 AUG 93 ACCESSIONED ON  17 AUG 93 at 10 15 CLINICAL DATA  Status post right mastectomy REMOVED_DATE                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  PREDOMINANTLY COMEDO TYPE  FOCALLY ABUTTING UPON THE MARGIN  LEVELS EXAMINED  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  19 AUG 93 at 17 18                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 AUG 93 at 08 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  