 gray yellow calcification within the dense gray white fibrous tissue  0 9cm from the cavity and 1 4cm from the closest posterior margin in the mid to inferior portion of the specimen  Another cluster of gritty tan yellow calcifications measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  and is located inferior to the first  0 4cm from the closest medial margin  and 1 7cm from the cavity  The remaining fibrous tissue shows focal nodularity with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the cavity to closest margins as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The first calcified focus is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the second as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections along the posterior and posteromedial aspect of the cavity  the region corresponding to the margin of concern in the prior excision  are submitted from superior to inferior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by John H Eichhorn M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by John H Eichhorn M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  This case was reviewed again  and at the request of the patient  who is a physician  additional tissue from the specimen was submitted for processing in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   A single duct in profile within the biopsy cavity wall on one of the eight additional slides shows residual ductal carcinoma in situ  and this tiny focus is 1 0cm from a blue inked margin  anterior   No stromal or lymphatic invasion is identified in the additional sections  Fibrocystic changes  harboring calcifications  are again noted  Addendum  1 by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT  RE  EXCISION , Unchecked.
