nd a long suture denoting the  lateral  aspect of the specimen  as per the surgeon  The specimen is inked for orientation as follows  superior  green  inferior  yellow  anterior blue  and posterior  black  Sectioning reveals a ragged  hemorrhagic cavity  2 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm   containing white  gritty material  consistent with packing material  This area is consistent with a previous biopsy site and is located 0 4cm from the anterior aspect  1 0cm from the superior aspect  0 6cm from the posterior aspect  1 0cm from the medial aspect  and focally abutting the inferolateral aspect of the specimen  The remaining cut surfaces consist of fibrous  focally nodular tissue with a scant amount of yellow  lobulated adipose tissue  The specimen is submitted in toto in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Body  submitted sequentially from medial to lateral  each cassette contains one half of a full thickness section    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin  serially sectioned  Received are six containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast anterior final margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the  new  margin  The surface containing the stitch is inked black  specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final lateral margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the  new  margin   The surface containing the stitch is inked black  specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final medial margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of tan yellow lobulated fibroadi