Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 13 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  WITH FOCAL SPINDLE CELL METAPLASIA  REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODE  INTRAMAMMARY   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 19 OF 19 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 06 46 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm overlying skin ellipse and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The superior border of the skin ellipse is marked with a stitch  A 1 0cm in diameter  brown plaque is located at 6 0cm lateral and superior to the nipple  overlying a firm mass below the skin  The resection margins are inked black  the anterior superior resection surface is double inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE tan to white  firm mass located beneath the skin lesion that extends to within 0 2cm of the posterior resection margin  The mass has a 1 0cm diameter irregular shaped cystic cavity containing white mucoid fluids  A 2 0cm in diameter white nodular mass is located at 5 0cm lateral to the first lesion  and appears well circumscribed  extends to within 0 2cm from the posterior resection margin  The second mass is located directly beneath the lateral end of the skin ellipse  at the base of the axillary tail  Section code  A  first mass at its closest resection margin  deep  B  first mass at skin C and D  sections taken from the medial and the lateral portion of the first mass  respectively E  second mass at its nearest resection margin  deep  F  the medial most section of the second mass G  the lateral most section of the second mass H L  nodes from axillary tail Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSIO