th this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 35     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  and unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm breast lumpectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm overlying skin ellipse  A short stitch is designated superior  a long stitch is designated lateral  Blue ink is applied laterally  Black inked is applied medially  The specimen is sectioned superior to inferior to reveal a 3 0cm nodule  adjacent to the medial posterior margin  which consists of firm  white parenchyma admixed with focal  white tan  gritty tissue  A representative section of the gritty tissue is frozen as FX  1  The remainder is submitted as follows  Section Code A   tissue adjacent to frozen section B F   entirety of the nodule G   superior resection margin  en face H I K L M   parenchyma 1cm inferior to nodule and 1cm superior to inferior resection margin J   inferior resection margin  en face N O   parenchyma 1cm superior to nodule but 1cm inferior from superior resection margin P   FX